  "findings": [
    "Four worked storage glyph hues connect glyphs, Unicode numbers and all their byte cells; é owns both C3 and A9 in glyph-correspondence views.",
    "Unicode NFC equivalence keeps the displayed-group hue; scientist scalars/11 bytes remain one group; NFKC ﬁ creates separate f/i groups with appropriate distinct hues. Native 48-ligature expansion displays 96 groups and correct counts.",
    "Byte-BPE numeric columns remain aligned and glyph-coloured in every rank; separate learned-piece brackets can have different hues before merging. Final phone DOM and compiled keys confirm both C3/A9 numeric cells blue.",
    "Regrouping explicitly follows byte-value identity; white boundary is separate from hue. Streaming same-glyph delivery/buffer/output matching survives null, inside-scalar and truncated states.",
    "Patch hues connect bytes, feature rows, groups and global/causal context. White selection/threshold remains readable. Probability, entropy, causal masks and scores retain semantic violet; bit payload roles are unchanged.",
    "Targeted desktop, 390px and 768px/200% views are readable, with no clipped labels or diagram paint failure found."
  ],
  "limits": "18 targeted predecessor captures and eight current captures were personally opened; this is not a claim to have reopened all 84 captured predecessor states. Seven renewed drawings plus the separate phone merge diagnostic are image-byte identical to their named predecessors. Exact worked helper style equality is separately proven. Root owns independent module-wide current build/reader/paint closure."
